---
title: Deviled Bacon and Eggs
description: The yolks get whipped in a stand mixer with a little cream, and peppered bacon goes on each half.
tags: [auntie-jeanie]
course: side
icons: [egg, bacon, pepper-hot]
cuisine: American
author: Ree Drummond
source:
  name: Food Network
  url: https://www.foodnetwork.com/recipes/ree-drummond/deviled-bacon-and-eggs-4489324
adapted: true
difficulty: easy
yield: 24%deviled eggs
time: 35m
---

Fry the @peppered bacon{6%slices} in a #pan{} over medium heat until crisp, ~fry{12-15%minutes}. Remove to a paper-lined plate.

Fill a large #pot{} with enough water to cover the eggs, then bring to a boil without the eggs. Using a #slotted spoon{}, gently lower the @eggs{12} into the boiling water. Cover and simmer for ~simmer{10%minutes}. Run the eggs under cold water until completely cooled.

> **Peeling** — Other kitchens cool the eggs in ice water instead. [America's Test Kitchen](https://www.americastestkitchen.com/recipes/570-classic-deviled-eggs) leaves them in an ice bath for 15 minutes. [Once Upon a Chef](https://www.onceuponachef.com/recipes/deviled-eggs.html) cracks them all over and peels under cool running water, starting at the wide end.

> **Spare Eggs** — Whites tear. [America's Test Kitchen](https://www.americastestkitchen.com/recipes/570-classic-deviled-eggs) cooks one egg more than it needs, uses every yolk, and discards the two worst-looking white halves.

Peel the @&eggs{}, cut them in half, and scoop the yolks into the bowl of a #stand mixer{} fitted with the whisk attachment. Add the @mayonnaise{1/4%cup}(59 ml), a little @heavy cream{}, the @yellow mustard{1%tsp}, a pinch of @sugar{1%pinch}, and the @white vinegar{1%tsp}. Add @hot sauce{}(such as Tabasco), @kosher salt{}, and @black pepper{}(freshly ground) to taste. Whip until smooth.

Using a small spoon, fill each egg white half with a generous teaspoon of the filling. Lightly sprinkle with @paprika{}. Cut the @&peppered bacon{} into chunks and top each egg half with a shard of bacon.

> **Making Ahead** — [America's Test Kitchen](https://www.americastestkitchen.com/recipes/570-classic-deviled-eggs) refrigerates the empty whites and the filling separately, tightly wrapped, for up to 2 days, then fills the eggs close to serving. [Alex Guarnaschelli](https://www.foodnetwork.com/recipes/deviled-eggs-with-bacon-and-hot-sauce-5519461) refrigerates her filled eggs and tops them with the bacon just before serving.

> **What's Changed** — Auntie Jeanie's handwritten note calls for a pinch of sugar where the original has 1 teaspoon, and a little cream where it has 1/4 cup.
